tical Stadium d’Île-de-France"] ", in Vaires-sur-Marne."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The dominant paddler at Paris 2024 was Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/123753"} "Jess Fox"] ", who won gold medals in both kayak and Canadian singles. She was also favored in the kayak cross but struggled and finished only 26th. In her fifth Olympics, this brought Fox’s medal total to six medals and three gold medals, both the best of all-time for the discipline, although her three gold medals are equaled by " [:a {:href "/athletes/90175"} "Tony Estanguet"] " (FRA) and the Slovakian Hochschorner brothers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/90262"} "Pavel"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/90263"} "Peter"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008412"} "Kayak Cross, Slalom, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  5 August 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "38"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008400"} "Kayak Singles, Slalom, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July –  1 August 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "24"] "\n" [:td {} "24"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008406"} "Canadian Singles, Slalom, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "27 – 29 July 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008437"} "Kayak Singles, Slalom, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "27 – 28 July 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008443"} "Canadian Singles, Slalom, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 – 31 July 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2008449"} "Kayak Cross, Slalom, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympi